      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Addition of $\\mathrm{H}-\\mathrm{Br}_{(\\mathrm{aq})}$ to alkene follows electrophilic addition mechanism. In the rate determining step a carbocation intermediate is formed. Among $\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{Q}$, R \\& S compound Q will form most stable carbocation intermediate since it is resonance stabilized.\n\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/OmDZb8mAnORkTQL_FzLcrPg1MkWTZ4qvYk1eornrp9Y.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
